                "Compiling the Three Layers of Unadjusted Misstatement: Under ISA 450 paragraph A3, the SUD stratifies audit misstatements into three distinct legal categories: Category 1: Factual Misstatements: Objective, indisputable errors identified in tested items (e.g., an unrecorded liability or duplicate invoice); Category 2: Projected Misstatements: The auditor's statistical projection of misstatements uncovered in audit samples across uninspected populations under ISA 530; Category 3: Judgmental Misstatements: Differences arising from management accounting estimates that the auditor considers unreasonable, or the inappropriate selection or application of accounting policies under ISA 540.",
